  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">World Federation Against Drugs (CSO strategin 2025-2029)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Federation Against Drugs (CSO strategy 2025-2029)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet, &#x201d;Voices for change: Empowering Youth and Civil Society for Inclusive Prevention and Reintigration&#x201d; fokuserar p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer och marginaliserade ungdomar (15&#x2013;29 &#xe5;r) i &#xd6;stafrika f&#xf6;r att leda r&#xe4;ttighetsbaserade och h&#xe5;llbara insatser inom f&#xf6;rebyggande arbete, &#xe5;terh&#xe4;mtning och &#xe5;terintegrering kopplat till substansmissbruk/beroende och kriminalitet. Projektet har ett extra fokus p&#xe5; unga kvinnor. Genom kapacitetsutveckling, ungas delaktighet, p&#xe5;verkansarbete och regionalt samarbete ska projektet bidra till inkluderande samh&#xe4;llen, social integration, jobbskapande och l&#xe5;ngsiktig demokratisk utveckling. Projektet kommer implementeras i Demokratiska republiken Kongo, Uganda, Tanzania och Kenya.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project, &#x201c;Voices for Change: Empowering Youth and Civil Society for Inclusive Prevention and Reintegration,&#x201d; focuses on strengthening civil society organizations and marginalized youth (ages 15&#x2013;29) in East Africa to lead rights-based and sustainable initiatives in prevention, recovery, and reintegration related to substance abuse/addiction and criminality. The project places particular emphasis on young women. Through capacity building, youth participation, advocacy, and regional cooperation, the project aims to contribute to inclusive societies, social integration, job creation, and long-term democratic development. The project will be implemented in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Uganda, Tanzania, and Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
